    <!-- v1.4.0.34 FINAL: NO NuGet assembly references at all. Evidence chain that led here:
         v1.4.0.30 hand-injected netcore50 facades -> 81 CS0012/CS0234;
         v1.4.0.32 removed the UWP metapackage (its packages\netcore50 DLLs shadowed SDK
         facades) -> WMC1006 persisted;
         v1.4.0.33 clean tree (packages/obj/bin deleted, fresh restore) -> WMC1006/WMC9999
         STILL persisted with only Newtonsoft.Json + DocumentFormat.OpenXml (netstandard1.3)
         referenced. Root cause, verified byte-level against nuget.org assets: a
         .NETStandard,v1.3 compile-time closure demands the whole NETSTANDARD1.3 facade
         package graph (System.Runtime ref 4.0.20.0 etc.), which no UAP 15063 SDK install
         contains - XamlCompiler type universe fails on the first one it cannot resolve.
         Therefore both libs are REMOVED from the project:
           - Newtonsoft.Json      -> vendored zero-dependency Helpers\JsonSerializer.cs
           - DocumentFormat.OpenXml -> xlsx built directly as OPC zip via
             System.IO.Compression.ZipArchive (Windows SDK, no NuGet).
         The compile universe is now ONLY Windows SDK reference assemblies + Platform.winmd,
         exactly like an untouched VS2017 UWP template - the configuration in which
         System.Runtime 4.0.0.0 always resolves. No HintPath references may be added back;
         if a third-party lib is ever needed again, it MUST ship a netcore50 or
         uap10.0-targeted asset (see BUILD_VS2017.md section "Зависимости"). -->
  </ItemGroup>
